Hello,

Welcome to the Accessibility Guidelines Working Group!

This email provides information and links to help you begin contributing to the work of the group.

The place to start is the "onboarding for new group members" page in the working group wiki:

  https://www.w3.org/WAI/GL/wiki/Onboarding_for_new_group_members

This provides links to much more information on participating in the working group.

You should start receiving emails from the working group list. This can have quite a lot of traffic – we would advise setting up a folder to filter this into. The email address is: w3c-wai-gl@w3.org.

The key emails to keep an eye out for are the weekly agenda emails. The subject lines are is in the format: "AGENDA - AGWG Meeting [Date]".

The onboarding wiki page includes information on the group's regular meetings. If and when you do join a call, it is customary for new members to give a quick introduction. For example, “I’m [name], I work for [company] doing [role], and I’m joining because I’m interested in…”. This is a standing point on the agenda so just let the chair know that you are in the meeting and wish to introduce yourself.

If you need accessibility accommodations to participate in the work, please let us know, with enough lead time to implement them.

All participants are required to follow the W3C Code of Conduct:
  https://www.w3.org/policies/code-of-conduct/

If you are joining as an Invited Expert, note that your status depends on ongoing active participation in the group. If you become inactive for 6 months or more, your Invited Expert status may not be extended. 

If you have have any questions about participating in the group, please get in touch with the chairs and staff contacts by email to group-ag-chairs@w3.org.

Kind regards,

